WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.536 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:04.870
[ Stopwatch beeps ]

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:07.907
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:14.847 --> 00:00:18.184
-I have been told a Negroni
is not a Negroni

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:21.087
unless it has an orange slice.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.688
So I ordered one.

00:00:22.688 --> 00:00:26.226
Not sure if it will make it here
before the end of "Corrections."

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:29.996
I am confused
about something.

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:31.764
I read the "Correction"
comments every week,

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:34.968
and people often will ask
questions that have been

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:38.004
answered within the body
of a previous "Corrections."

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:39.772
People will say,
"What is he drinking?"

00:00:39.772 --> 00:00:44.377
I've said Negroni
in multiple "Corrections."

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:46.379
How are you not watching
all of these?

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:48.214
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:54.086
Like, it doesn't work if you
don't watch all of these.

00:00:54.086 --> 00:00:55.287
"Do you watch
'Game of Thrones'?"

00:00:55.287 --> 00:00:57.357
"Well, I catch it when it's on."
What?

00:00:57.357 --> 00:01:00.793
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.793 --> 00:01:05.598
You got to watch all of these.

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:07.299
So many of the questions --

00:01:07.299 --> 00:01:08.935
What am I drinking?
A Negroni.

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:11.838
"Did you know Doug Jones was
the original Mac Tonight?"

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:12.672
I do.

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:14.107
Why are shows --

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:16.242
Why is "Closer Look"
not on in Canada anymore?

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:17.911
Because you're bad listeners.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:20.213
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:27.020
Uh, I was told VHS tapes
don't play backwards

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.956
if you put them
in upside down.

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:33.192
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:34.727
Agree to disagree.

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:37.262
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.262 --> 00:01:41.601
Last week,
I called out Sal Gentile

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.703
and said he was wrong
in his interpretation

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:50.543
of the landmark Supreme Court
case Marbury v. Madison.

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:53.546
Sal was right, it turns out.

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:55.148
But by calling him
out in "Corrections,"

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:57.883
I did inadvertently get Sal

00:01:57.883 --> 00:02:01.553
into the Guinness Book
of World's Records

00:02:01.553 --> 00:02:03.489
for "Longest Mutter."

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:06.692
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.692 --> 00:02:08.527
[ Muttering ] Huh?
What are you talkin' about?

00:02:08.527 --> 00:02:12.265
[ Muttering indistinctly ]

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:13.532
Really had to talk Sal off --

00:02:13.532 --> 00:02:14.967
He wanted to write
a "Closer Look"

00:02:14.967 --> 00:02:16.202
about YouTube commenters.

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.871
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:25.410
We talked about
Scooby-Doo last week

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:27.679
and how he said "Ruh-ro."

00:02:27.679 --> 00:02:30.249
I was told by many of you

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:35.053
Astro from "The Jetsons"
was the originator of "Ruh-ro."

00:02:35.053 --> 00:02:36.890
Interesting fact here.

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:43.863
The actor who did Astro would
later go on to voice Scooby-Doo.

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:48.934
And that must have been a very
weird call from his agent.

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:51.671
He's like, "Hey, baby, I got you
the lead in a new pilot,"

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:53.439
and he's like,
"Oh, that's great.

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:55.741
Anything as long as I'm not
doing another cartoon dog,

00:02:55.741 --> 00:02:58.878
if you know what I mean."

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:04.217
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:05.585
"You still there?"

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:09.088
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:12.692
"Ruh-ro."

00:03:15.928 --> 00:03:17.029
This is a correction

00:03:17.029 --> 00:03:20.566
I had a hard time
wrapping my head around.

00:03:20.566 --> 00:03:23.002
Correction --
Scooby-Doo isn't a dog.

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.470
In later seasons, it established

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:29.008
that Scooby is actually
an alien known as an Anunnaki,

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:31.610
a race of ancient creatures
that can cross universes

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:35.615
and take over
the form of animals.

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:39.018
I'm not sure what season
that plot point was established,

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:40.519
but I'm...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:42.588
I'm gonna guess the last one.

00:03:42.588 --> 00:03:47.093
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:49.261
"Ratings are down.

00:03:49.261 --> 00:03:51.631
Should we throw this [bleep]
Hail Mary?"

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.198
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.198 --> 00:03:55.535
"Kids like space, right?"

00:04:02.074 --> 00:04:04.243
Last week, I addressed
one of you said

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:06.312
my Shaggy impression
sounded like Werner Herzog.

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:09.315
I put that to bed.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:10.950
But then one of you
this week said,

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:14.254
when you heard me say my Shaggy
sounded like Werner Herzog,

00:04:14.254 --> 00:04:16.956
you thought it was
the singer Shaggy.

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:19.425
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:21.494
[ As Werner Herzog ]
It wasn't me.

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:24.630
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.799
Yes, you caught me
on ze counter.

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:29.268
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.268 --> 00:04:32.571
It wasn't me.

00:04:32.571 --> 00:04:35.574
I believe you believe

00:04:35.574 --> 00:04:37.577
you saw me
banging on the sofa.

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:40.679
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.679 --> 00:04:44.217
But it wasn't me.

00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:47.820
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:51.024
[ Normal voice ] A lot of you
said Jacob Marley is a ghost.

00:04:51.024 --> 00:04:54.092
The other three are spirits.

00:04:54.092 --> 00:04:56.929
Can you really tell
the difference between a spirit

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:58.964
and a ghost?

00:04:58.964 --> 00:05:01.066
I know you can tell
the difference between a spirit

00:05:01.066 --> 00:05:03.136
and a JetBlue.

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:06.939
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:08.808
Baze, I did it
just like you said.

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:12.444
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.444 --> 00:05:15.348
"Then lean forward
like you're proud of it."

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:20.519
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.519 --> 00:05:22.855
It's Thanksgiving,
not April Fools, Baze.

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:25.191
[ Laughter ]

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:29.061
Um...

00:05:29.061 --> 00:05:30.829
You know, there's a --

00:05:30.829 --> 00:05:32.464
We've been talking about Devon,

00:05:32.464 --> 00:05:36.435
the 28-year-old teenager
who turns up a lot on our show.

00:05:36.435 --> 00:05:37.770
He turned up twice in a week,

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:41.773
and then one of you said,
"I think he --

00:05:41.773 --> 00:05:43.876
I think you've used him
more than just a few times."

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:47.079
And, you know,
there's this consensus...

00:05:47.079 --> 00:05:48.948
building that young people
don't like to work anymore.

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:51.583
But let me tell you
something about this kid.

00:05:51.583 --> 00:05:54.053
Does a shift at DQ...

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:56.622
then he goes over
to Burger King...

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:57.990
then he goes to Chipotle...

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:00.192
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.192 --> 00:06:02.761
...then he
heads over to Kinko's.

00:06:02.761 --> 00:06:05.665
Yeah, sure.
Then he toilet-papers my house.

00:06:05.665 --> 00:06:09.234
But next morning,
he's at the amusement park.

00:06:09.234 --> 00:06:12.004
Then it's off
to Dunkin' Donuts...

00:06:12.004 --> 00:06:14.140
Best Buy...

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:16.275
then he breaks
his [bleep] leg...

00:06:16.275 --> 00:06:18.110
[ Laughter ]

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:20.445
...and then,
it's over to 7-Eleven.

00:06:20.445 --> 00:06:22.281
Thank you for your work, Devon.

00:06:22.281 --> 00:06:24.884
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:26.051
Someone, uh --

00:06:26.051 --> 00:06:27.720
Someone wrote this comment --

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:28.921
"This show sucks.

00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:31.123
He must be paying
that phony audience to laugh.

00:06:31.123 --> 00:06:34.160
Sounds like about 10 people,
LOL."

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.660
[ Laughter ]

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:37.396
First of all, dude...

00:06:37.396 --> 00:06:40.333
[ Laughter ]

00:06:40.333 --> 00:06:43.269
...it used to be 10, but then
we let the interns start coming,

00:06:43.269 --> 00:06:44.704
and it's 16.

00:06:44.704 --> 00:06:48.340
[ Laughter ]

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:49.809
I was actually worried
our audience

00:06:49.809 --> 00:06:51.110
would be a little thin today

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:52.712
because, you know,
a lot of our crew

00:06:52.712 --> 00:06:56.248
has left to get to the airport
for the holiday.

00:06:56.248 --> 00:07:00.419
We have a diverse crew from
all over the country,

00:07:00.419 --> 00:07:02.655
everywhere from
the top of New Jersey

00:07:02.655 --> 00:07:04.056
to the middle of Long Island.

00:07:04.056 --> 00:07:06.058
[ Laughter ]

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:08.227
Oh.
Thank you.

00:07:15.401 --> 00:07:17.536
Ah. Yeah.

00:07:17.536 --> 00:07:19.572
[ Laughter ]

00:07:22.608 --> 00:07:26.479
[ Laughter ]

00:07:33.352 --> 00:07:35.821
"Hey, honey?"
"What?"

00:07:35.821 --> 00:07:39.792
"You know how you say I'm never
gonna sell my old cans on eBay?"

00:07:39.792 --> 00:07:42.661
[ Laughter ]

00:07:42.661 --> 00:07:46.299
"Well, I just sold one
to a talk-show host."

00:07:46.299 --> 00:07:49.601
[ Laughter ]

00:07:49.601 --> 00:07:52.705
"My ship came in, baby!"

00:07:52.705 --> 00:07:54.840
[ Laughter ]

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:57.910
$6, plus shipping.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:00.246
[ Laughter ]

00:08:06.952 --> 00:08:09.321
Oh, we just mentioned
New Jersey.

00:08:09.321 --> 00:08:12.558
We mentioned Trump looked like
a tiger in a podunk zoo

00:08:12.558 --> 00:08:14.526
in Central New Jersey.
A lot of you got mad.

00:08:14.526 --> 00:08:16.729
You said it's either
Northern New Jersey

00:08:16.729 --> 00:08:20.666
or Southern new Jersey.
I was purposefully vague

00:08:20.666 --> 00:08:23.869
about where in New Jersey
this podunk zoo was,

00:08:23.869 --> 00:08:25.471
because the last thing I wanted

00:08:25.471 --> 00:08:30.175
was some actual Jersey zookeeper
taking offense.

00:08:30.175 --> 00:08:31.710
You know, I don't need
one of them

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:34.480
waiting outside the building
when I walk out, and he's like,

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:35.781
"Who's podunk now?"

00:08:35.781 --> 00:08:37.950
and throws a bunch
of salamanders on me.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:41.454
[ Laughter ]

00:08:44.523 --> 00:08:48.360
[ Laughter ]

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:50.462
Two years ago, I announced
the birth of our daughter

00:08:50.462 --> 00:08:51.898
on Thanksgiving "Corrections,"

00:08:51.898 --> 00:08:56.302
and I told the story about
how her first name is Adelaide,

00:08:56.302 --> 00:08:58.337
which is my grandmother's name

00:08:58.337 --> 00:09:00.773
and why that was such
an important name for us.

00:09:00.773 --> 00:09:03.509
And I forgot to mention
that her middle name is Ruth,

00:09:03.509 --> 00:09:05.878
which is my wife's
grandmother's name.

00:09:05.878 --> 00:09:08.147
And then I showed
on Thanksgiving.

00:09:08.147 --> 00:09:12.951
I showed the "Corrections"
to my family and and my in-laws.

00:09:12.951 --> 00:09:14.853
And my wife took me
aside afterwards to go,

00:09:14.853 --> 00:09:16.922
"I think it really
hurt my feelings

00:09:16.922 --> 00:09:18.324
that you would forget
to say the Ruth part."

00:09:18.324 --> 00:09:19.891
And I was like,
"Oh, my God, I'm so sorry.

00:09:19.891 --> 00:09:21.126
It just slipped my mind."

00:09:21.126 --> 00:09:22.594
And so last year's "Corrections"
on Thanksgiving,

00:09:22.594 --> 00:09:25.598
I corrected the record, and I
said her middle name was Ruth.

00:09:25.598 --> 00:09:27.499
And I told that story
independently.

00:09:27.499 --> 00:09:28.900
And then I told her,

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:31.070
assuming she would say,
"Good job. You fixed it,"

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:32.738
but instead she said, "I don't
think people pay attention.

00:09:32.738 --> 00:09:34.507
I think they only pay
attention the first time.

00:09:34.507 --> 00:09:35.874
And I think -- I think
they pay attention.

00:09:35.874 --> 00:09:38.277
I think everybody knows now
her name's Adelaide Ruth,

00:09:38.277 --> 00:09:39.745
and we can just
put it behind us."

00:09:39.745 --> 00:09:43.315
True story -- the other day,
my oldest son said to the Alexa,

00:09:43.315 --> 00:09:46.719
"Alexa, what are
Seth Meyers' kids' names?"

00:09:46.719 --> 00:09:49.321
and Alexa said,
"Seth Meyers has three children.

00:09:49.321 --> 00:09:51.356
Their names
are Ashe Olson Meyers,

00:09:51.356 --> 00:09:54.326
Axel Strahl Meyers,
Adelaide Meyers."

00:09:54.326 --> 00:09:57.763
[ Laughter ]

00:09:57.763 --> 00:09:59.598
And I said, "Alexa,
how do you not know that?"

00:09:59.598 --> 00:10:02.301
And she said, "I don't
watch every 'Corrections.'"

00:10:02.301 --> 00:10:05.338
[ Laughter ]

00:10:10.543 --> 00:10:12.945
Security guard John O'Malley

00:10:12.945 --> 00:10:15.181
won the "Corrections" pool
last week.

00:10:15.181 --> 00:10:18.150
Wasn't even here.
[ Laughter ]

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:19.418
So the saddest thing happened,

00:10:19.418 --> 00:10:22.688
which is Jim had to call
and give him the good news.

00:10:22.688 --> 00:10:24.390
[ Laughter ]

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:26.291
Poor Jim had to deliver it to --

00:10:26.291 --> 00:10:28.994
O'Malley, who wins this thing,
I feel like, every other week.

00:10:28.994 --> 00:10:31.363
O'Malley's walking out of here
with a handful of cash.

00:10:31.363 --> 00:10:33.398
[ Laughter ]

00:10:33.398 --> 00:10:35.101
Still surprised every time
he wins.

00:10:35.101 --> 00:10:36.969
'Cause I saw him on Monday,
I was like, "Congratulations."

00:10:36.969 --> 00:10:38.336
"I couldn't believe it, Seth."

00:10:38.336 --> 00:10:39.705
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:39.705 --> 00:10:41.873
"I mean..."

00:10:41.873 --> 00:10:43.943
[ Laughter continues ]

00:10:43.943 --> 00:10:46.345
"...I'm sitting at home,
I get a phone call from Jim.

00:10:46.345 --> 00:10:49.281
I'm like,
'Is there an emergency?'

00:10:49.281 --> 00:10:51.316
So, I pick up the phone.

00:10:51.316 --> 00:10:55.321
Jim gives me the news.
I'm excited. Jim's excited.

00:10:55.321 --> 00:10:57.123
Yeah, I was over the moon."

00:10:57.123 --> 00:11:00.258
[ Laughter ]

00:11:00.258 --> 00:11:01.927
"I mean, I'm winning
at this pool,

00:11:01.927 --> 00:11:04.396
so I feel like I'm as good
at pools

00:11:04.396 --> 00:11:06.331
as my daughter Katie is
at field hockey."

00:11:06.331 --> 00:11:10.902
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:11:10.902 --> 00:11:13.472
John is very proud
of his children.

00:11:13.472 --> 00:11:15.073
[ Laughter ]

00:11:15.073 --> 00:11:18.110
I am certain that if John is
ever on duty

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:19.645
when I'm attacked...

00:11:19.645 --> 00:11:22.581
[ Laughter ]

00:11:22.581 --> 00:11:24.950
...the assailant will get by
because he will be showing

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:27.987
a picture of one of his children
to a stranger on his phone.

00:11:27.987 --> 00:11:31.457
[ Laughter ]

00:11:34.593 --> 00:11:38.164
Uh, we did our 50th
"Jokes Seth Can't Tell"

00:11:38.164 --> 00:11:40.332
on Tuesday.
Jenny and Amber surprised me.

00:11:40.332 --> 00:11:43.502
They changed the format
to celebrate the 50th.

00:11:43.502 --> 00:11:46.305
A lot of jackals
asked questions about this.

00:11:46.305 --> 00:11:48.206
One was,
"Was Seth really surprised?"

00:11:48.206 --> 00:11:50.308
I definitely
was really surprised.

00:11:50.308 --> 00:11:52.478
Next question was,
"Was he really angry?"

00:11:52.478 --> 00:11:53.879
I was not really angry,

00:11:53.879 --> 00:11:56.014
but I did feel, for the purposes
of the comedy,

00:11:56.014 --> 00:11:58.350
I should play as though
I was a little bit angry

00:11:58.350 --> 00:11:59.518
that they had pulled
one over on me,

00:11:59.518 --> 00:12:01.119
which they had
effectively done.

00:12:01.119 --> 00:12:03.789
I wasn't angry
because I felt safe,

00:12:03.789 --> 00:12:08.560
because Amber and Jenny
are very kind, very empathetic

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:11.063
comedy writers, and I knew
that they would not --

00:12:11.063 --> 00:12:12.998
they would go
right up to the line

00:12:12.998 --> 00:12:15.200
without actually crossing it
and putting me in a situation

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:16.535
where I could get myself
in trouble.

00:12:16.535 --> 00:12:18.136
So that was
the nice part about it.

00:12:18.136 --> 00:12:19.471
Now, if there was
a surprise sketch

00:12:19.471 --> 00:12:21.874
where I found out in real time
that Mike Scollins

00:12:21.874 --> 00:12:24.844
had written stuff...
[ Laughter ]

00:12:24.844 --> 00:12:26.044
...that I had to read on --

00:12:26.044 --> 00:12:27.880
I would know
my career is over.

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:30.548
[ Laughter ]

00:12:30.548 --> 00:12:32.051
[ As Werner Herzog ]
It was me.

00:12:32.051 --> 00:12:34.819
[ Laughter ]

00:12:34.819 --> 00:12:37.022
I don't want to keep up
this charade any more.

00:12:37.022 --> 00:12:38.991
[ Laughter ]

00:12:38.991 --> 00:12:41.026
You even caught me on camera.

00:12:41.026 --> 00:12:44.462
[ Laughter ]

00:12:44.462 --> 00:12:47.599
I blame myself.

00:12:47.599 --> 00:12:50.402
How could I forget
I'd given you the extra key?

00:12:50.402 --> 00:12:53.005
[ Laughter ]

00:12:59.011 --> 00:13:00.646
[ Normal voice ]
Well...

00:13:05.217 --> 00:13:09.321
[ Laughter ]

00:13:09.321 --> 00:13:10.789
I, uh -- I --

00:13:10.789 --> 00:13:12.191
Happy Thanksgiving, everybody.

00:13:12.191 --> 00:13:15.227
This is genuinely such a special
part of the week for me.

00:13:15.227 --> 00:13:19.131
And I really like that
you're here for this every week.

00:13:19.131 --> 00:13:23.335
I really like that I get to be
here and do this every week.

00:13:23.335 --> 00:13:25.704
It's a very special thing
to share with my crew.

00:13:25.704 --> 00:13:31.276
It's extra special tonight
because there are people here

00:13:31.276 --> 00:13:32.745
[voice breaking] who mean a
great deal to me

00:13:32.745 --> 00:13:34.847
that aren't always here,
and they know who they are.

00:13:34.847 --> 00:13:35.847
[ Sniffles ]

00:13:35.847 --> 00:13:37.883
And, uh...

00:13:40.752 --> 00:13:44.456
[ Laughter ]
[ Sniffles ]

00:13:44.456 --> 00:13:47.793
Well...
[ Sniffles ]

00:13:47.793 --> 00:13:50.662
[ Stopwatch beeps ]

00:13:50.662 --> 00:13:51.863
Kenny won.

00:13:51.863 --> 00:13:54.499
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:13:54.499 --> 00:13:56.701
Or at least you would have
if it was over now.

00:13:56.701 --> 00:14:00.172
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:14:03.842 --> 00:14:05.811
Will the show pay for this?

00:14:05.811 --> 00:14:08.280
[ Laughter ]

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:14.220
See me next two weeks.

